WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.099 --> 00:00:13.580
There are thousand ways to overthrow a dictator: from violent revolutions to peaceful transitions…

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:17.020
but Venezuela is trying something unique.

00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:20.680
Its parliament has just named an alternative
president to Nicolas Maduro.

00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:24.430
His name is Juan GUAIDO (((gw-eye-doe))))
and he’s the man who will lead the country

00:00:24.430 --> 00:00:29.039
into democracy… if he can actually pull
it off.

00:00:29.039 --> 00:00:34.870
Because, let’s be clear here…

00:00:34.870 --> 00:00:38.180
Venezuela is now under a dictatorship: Nicolas
Maduro’s dictatorship.

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:41.309
And yes, yes, I know what you might be thinking…

00:00:41.309 --> 00:00:42.309
Come on, Simon!

00:00:42.309 --> 00:00:45.390
How can this be a dictatorship if they hold
elections?

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:46.719
Of course they do!

00:00:46.719 --> 00:00:50.129
People can vote in Bangladesh, Egypt, and
Azerbaijan too.

00:00:50.129 --> 00:00:53.899
Even in North Korea they have legislative
elections every 5 years.

00:00:53.899 --> 00:00:56.370
And people can even choose among different
political parties, too.

00:00:56.370 --> 00:00:59.170
No, I’m not being sarcastic: Google it!

00:00:59.170 --> 00:01:05.240
But look, if you wanna have democracy, elections
must be free and fair and, of course, you

00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:06.530
need freedom of speech.

00:01:06.530 --> 00:01:14.979
And freedom of speech in Venezuela is as scarce
as toilet paper.

00:01:14.979 --> 00:01:19.469
Basically, all the websites that are critical
of the government are banned, and that includes

00:01:19.469 --> 00:01:22.110
those using a link shortener like BIT.LY.

00:01:22.110 --> 00:01:27.060
Most of the TVs are nationalized or owned
by friends of the government and oppositional

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:31.560
newspapers cannot be printed because the paper
industry is a monopoly held by the government.

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:34.259
And yes, yes, some of you might still say…

00:01:34.259 --> 00:01:39.090
But Maduro is very popular among his people,
isn’t he?

00:01:39.090 --> 00:01:40.090
Of course he is!

00:01:40.090 --> 00:01:43.320
In fact, every dictator in history was beloved
by his people.

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:46.990
See, the 101st lesson in the dictator’s
playbook is: never stop spending on propaganda.

00:01:46.990 --> 00:01:48.350
And what does lesson 102 say?

00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:50.509
‘Send all of your enemies to prison!’.

00:01:50.509 --> 00:01:55.619
Once you have the courts in your pocket, it’s
easy to accuse anybody of all kinds of crimes.

00:01:55.619 --> 00:01:59.390
In arab dictatorships, they usually claim
their opponents are terrorists.

00:01:59.390 --> 00:02:02.710
In Maduro’s Venezuela, they just label them
conspirators.

00:02:02.710 --> 00:02:10.929
But, OK, now you might say “Sure, Simon,
we get it, Maduro is a dictator but… proclaiming

00:02:10.929 --> 00:02:13.910
yourself as the legitimate president without
winning an election?

00:02:13.910 --> 00:02:15.530
Isn’t that a coup d’etat?

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:18.130
At least, that’s what many people are saying
nowadays…

00:02:18.130 --> 00:02:20.380
Well… in fact, the opposite is true.

00:02:20.380 --> 00:02:24.720
Listen, a coup d’etat is defined as the
taking of a government through the use of

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:29.860
force by a group that already has some kind
of power inside the system, usually, the military.

00:02:29.860 --> 00:02:34.250
But Juan GUAIDO is using an article in the
Venezuelan Constitution.

00:02:34.250 --> 00:02:39.610
Article 233 allows the president of the National
Assembly, that is, JUAN GUAIDO, to occupy,

00:02:39.610 --> 00:02:46.570
temporarily, the presidency of the Republic
if there is an absence of power.

00:02:46.570 --> 00:02:50.690
Since Maduro came to power by violating the
Constitution, there is no president now…

00:02:50.690 --> 00:02:52.050
from a legal point of view.

00:02:52.050 --> 00:02:56.760
So now, the brand new Venezuelan executive
has 30 days to call for new elections.

00:02:56.760 --> 00:03:01.450
So yes, Maduro’s opposition is overthrowing
a dictator by following the Constitution to

00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:02.450
the letter.

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:06.350
And this is why so many governments, including
Trump’s America and Trudeau’s Canada,

00:03:06.350 --> 00:03:10.480
have recognized Mr. Guaido as the legitimate
president of Venezuela.

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:13.570
But there is still a big question we have
to ask here.

00:03:13.570 --> 00:03:16.390
Is this good or bad news for Venezuela?

00:03:16.390 --> 00:03:19.030
Is it that easy to end a dictatorship?

00:03:19.030 --> 00:03:26.480
You just go, claim to be the president, wait
for America to recognize you and… that’s

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:27.500
it?

00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:33.130
Well… my dear viewers, the answer is no.

00:03:33.130 --> 00:03:37.780
If there’s a lesson we can learn from history
on this subject, it’s that even the countries

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:41.140
with the worst dictatorships can get even
worse.

00:03:41.140 --> 00:03:44.570
For example, Saddam’s Iraq or Gaddadi’s
Lybia.

00:03:44.570 --> 00:03:46.820
Is Venezuela heading toward the same fate?

00:03:46.820 --> 00:03:51.400
Are there reasons to be more optimistic about
Venezuela’s situation?

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:55.570
Today we are NOT going to answer these questions,
because it’s impossible to do that.

00:03:55.570 --> 00:03:58.750
But we are going to give you the keys to understand
them.

00:03:58.750 --> 00:04:05.290
But before we do, as always… let’s take
a look back at the history.

00:04:05.290 --> 00:04:07.430
THE END OF DEMOCRACY

00:04:07.430 --> 00:04:10.720
Remember this date: May 1st, 2017.

00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:15.480
In this moment, Venezuela’s parliament was
mostly made up of members of Maduro’s opposition

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:16.480
party.

00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:18.780
Of course, we aren’t just talking about
a party that opposed Maduro.

00:04:18.780 --> 00:04:22.570
In fact, there are many of those and they
range from left wing to right wing.

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:24.660
But nobody cares about them.

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:28.180
Since 2016, the Parliament had been declared
disrespectful.

00:04:28.180 --> 00:04:31.030
This means, they no longer had legal power.

00:04:31.030 --> 00:04:32.030
Why not?

00:04:32.030 --> 00:04:35.690
Well… because, according to the government,
there were 3 MPs that won the election in

00:04:35.690 --> 00:04:36.920
an unfair manner.

00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:39.260
What a surprise!

00:04:39.260 --> 00:04:44.950
3 MPs was the exact number that they needed
to avoid a 2 thirds majority in the congress.

00:04:44.950 --> 00:04:48.530
With a 2 thirds majority, the executive power
would be in dire straits.

00:04:48.530 --> 00:04:55.770
And this is why Nicolas Maduro finally acted
to, cripple the opposition.

00:04:55.770 --> 00:05:01.890
I’m summoning the constituent power to achieve
the peace this Republic needs!

00:05:01.890 --> 00:05:05.460
We need to destroy this fascist coup d’etat!

00:05:05.460 --> 00:05:14.850
We need the people, with their sovereignty,
to impose peace!

00:05:14.850 --> 00:05:18.680
This was the exact moment where Maduro declared
the parliament illegal.

00:05:18.680 --> 00:05:21.960
The only opposition he still had was, politically,
killed.

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:23.010
And what happened next?

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:25.650
Well, Basically, Maduro made up a brand new
parliament.

00:05:25.650 --> 00:05:27.580
The so called CONSTITUENCY ASSEMBLY.

00:05:27.580 --> 00:05:33.470
A parliament with 545 MPs where, surprise,
surprise, 503 were members of the Government’s

00:05:33.470 --> 00:05:34.470
party!

00:05:34.470 --> 00:05:38.890
Strange as this sounds, this movement could
still be considered legal according to Venezuela’s

00:05:38.890 --> 00:05:39.890
constitution.

00:05:39.890 --> 00:05:44.340
Article 348 says the president can create
a council to make a brand new constitution.

00:05:44.340 --> 00:05:45.340
The problem?

00:05:45.340 --> 00:05:49.750
Those MPs from the same political party were
making all kinds of laws, including tax laws.

00:05:49.750 --> 00:05:55.550
It was, in fact, a parallel parliament.

00:05:55.550 --> 00:06:00.180
In the meantime, the old parliament, with
different political parties, kept holding

00:06:00.180 --> 00:06:02.630
sessions but with no real power.

00:06:02.630 --> 00:06:05.520
The army and the police was on Maduro’s
side.

00:06:05.520 --> 00:06:11.040
This is when Venezuela went from being a kind
of sketchy democracy under financial collapse

00:06:11.040 --> 00:06:12.980
to… a classic dictatorship.

00:06:12.980 --> 00:06:16.060
But wait a minute because here’s the important
part.

00:06:16.060 --> 00:06:17.740
This fake parliament called for elections.

00:06:17.740 --> 00:06:22.030
As you can imagine, with nearly all of the
members belonging to the president’s political

00:06:22.030 --> 00:06:26.280
party, those elections were as predictable
as the ending of ‘The passion of the Christ’.

00:06:26.280 --> 00:06:28.450
Yes, you guessed it!

00:06:28.450 --> 00:06:30.180
Maduro won by a landslide.

00:06:30.180 --> 00:06:34.760
But, of course, no serious country recognized
the result of the elections.

00:06:34.760 --> 00:06:38.331
Already in 2018, Mike Pence, the American
Vice President, said this about Maduro.

00:06:38.331 --> 00:06:46.980
The United States has called this election
what it really was: a sham (…) Maduro must

00:06:46.980 --> 00:06:52.380
hold free and fair elections, and release
all political prisoners immediately and unconditionally.

00:06:52.380 --> 00:06:55.840
--Mike Pence, Vice President USA

00:06:55.840 --> 00:06:59.139
The same happened in most South American and
European countries.

00:06:59.139 --> 00:07:01.940
Nobody recognized the results of this election.

00:07:01.940 --> 00:07:02.940
The problem?

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:04.440
There was no alternative to Maduro’s rule.

00:07:04.440 --> 00:07:08.460
And this is how we got to January 2019, when
Maduro took office.

00:07:08.460 --> 00:07:12.910
Of course, he didn’t do it before the National
Assembly because he doesn’t like them.

00:07:12.910 --> 00:07:16.170
Instead, he took office in front of the Supreme
Court of Justice.

00:07:16.170 --> 00:07:19.990
According to the constitution, this means
he made his oath illegally, and therefore,

00:07:19.990 --> 00:07:21.730
he is an illegal president.

00:07:21.730 --> 00:07:22.730
And this was when the opposition, with the
law in their hands, could start putting their

00:07:22.730 --> 00:07:23.730
plans into play.

00:07:23.730 --> 00:07:26.540
Having no legitimate president, the president
of the National Assembly, Juan GUAIDO, made

00:07:26.540 --> 00:07:27.630
another oath.

00:07:27.630 --> 00:07:32.199
And this is when all those countries who didn’t
recognize the outcome of the elections started

00:07:32.199 --> 00:07:35.750
recognizing Guaido as the legitimate president
of Venezuela.

00:07:35.750 --> 00:07:40.120
But OK, maybe you’re now thinking… hmm…
just 5 minutes after Guaido made the oath,

00:07:40.120 --> 00:07:42.949
Trump recognized him…

00:07:42.949 --> 00:07:46.630
Is this pure chance, or was there a plan already
in place?

00:07:46.630 --> 00:07:50.010
Well, let’s take a look.

00:07:50.010 --> 00:07:51.310
WHO CARES ABOUT VENEZUELA?

00:07:51.310 --> 00:07:55.460
If you’ve been following VisualPolitik for
a long time, you already know that Venezuela

00:07:55.460 --> 00:07:59.660
is the country with the biggest oil reserves
on the planet: bigger than Saudi Arabia’s,

00:07:59.660 --> 00:08:00.949
Russia’s, or America’s.

00:08:00.949 --> 00:08:01.949
The problem?

00:08:01.949 --> 00:08:03.690
They can hardly make a profit off of them.

00:08:03.690 --> 00:08:06.490
You see, it’s one thing to have lots of
dinosaur juice.

00:08:06.490 --> 00:08:09.510
And it’s another entirely to make money
off of that dinosaur juice.

00:08:09.510 --> 00:08:14.919
Just have a look at this chart.

00:08:14.919 --> 00:08:19.400
Here you can see the production cost of an
oil barrel by country.

00:08:19.400 --> 00:08:22.419
Saudi Arabia has the cheapest cost per barrel.

00:08:22.419 --> 00:08:26.240
This is why, regarding the market price, they
always make a profit.

00:08:26.240 --> 00:08:28.800
Meanwhile, Venezuela is on the other side.

00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:31.639
They have one of the most expensive oil costs.

00:08:31.639 --> 00:08:41.659
And if this isn’t enough, PDVSA, the state
oil company, is in chaos.

00:08:41.659 --> 00:08:48.019
In other words, they can’t make money by
selling their oil at the market price.

00:08:48.019 --> 00:08:52.580
This is why, despite being the country with
the biggest oil reserves on the planet, Venezuela

00:08:52.580 --> 00:08:56.230
produces less oil than Angola or Nigeria.

00:08:56.230 --> 00:09:00.230
In fact, they represent just 7% of the oil
imports in America.

00:09:00.230 --> 00:09:04.370
This means their weight in the International
economy is pretty small.

00:09:04.370 --> 00:09:08.279
Especially at a time when America is surpassing
Saudi Arabia in oil production.

00:09:08.279 --> 00:09:10.930
Yes, America is no longer that crazy about
oil.

00:09:10.930 --> 00:09:13.999
On the other hand, Trump has already restricted
investments in Venezuela.

00:09:13.999 --> 00:09:18.050
This means, banks aren’t really exposed
to anything that happens in this country.

00:09:18.050 --> 00:09:21.300
They just don’t care about Venezuela.

00:09:21.300 --> 00:09:24.490
Of course, the White House still doesn’t
like Maduro.

00:09:24.490 --> 00:09:28.480
That’s why they’ve named ELLION ABRAMS
as the special envoy to Venezuela.

00:09:28.480 --> 00:09:33.139
Abrams was the guy behind the IRAN/CONTRA
scandal, as well as Venezuela’s coup against

00:09:33.139 --> 00:09:34.550
Chavez in 2002.

00:09:34.550 --> 00:09:39.160
But, let’s be honest… Trump has many other
things to think about besides Venezuela.

00:09:39.160 --> 00:09:43.360
In Spain and, generally, the Spanish speaking
world, Venezuela is on the front page of all

00:09:43.360 --> 00:09:44.480
the newspapers.

00:09:44.480 --> 00:09:47.759
Everybody talks about it in the bars and cafes
of Madrid.

00:09:47.759 --> 00:09:49.959
There is an actual debate between Maduro’s
supporters and Maduro’s opposers.

00:09:49.959 --> 00:09:54.240
But in America… well, you might know that
something has happened in Venezuela, but you

00:09:54.240 --> 00:09:56.180
probably aren’t too passionate about it.

00:09:56.180 --> 00:09:59.980
Nonetheless, guess which country has a bigger
stake in Venezuela!

00:09:59.980 --> 00:10:01.639
Here’s a hint.

00:10:01.639 --> 00:10:09.189
It starts with C and ends with…!!!

00:10:09.189 --> 00:10:15.800
China now taking 28% of Venezuela’s oil
production to repay debt

00:10:15.800 --> 00:10:19.160
As we said in previous videos, China needs
natural resources.

00:10:19.160 --> 00:10:21.450
So they made big loans to Venezuela.

00:10:21.450 --> 00:10:25.069
So far, Caracas owes Beijing more than 50
billion dollars.

00:10:25.069 --> 00:10:27.330
That’s the cost of 3 Olympic games.

00:10:27.330 --> 00:10:32.009
But, since Venezuela no longer has the money
to pay back their debts, they have to pay

00:10:32.009 --> 00:10:33.009
with oil.

00:10:33.009 --> 00:10:34.990
Still wondering why China still supports Maduro?

00:10:34.990 --> 00:10:37.290
Well, he’s the only one who can guarantee
the oil shipments.

00:10:37.290 --> 00:10:38.290
Who knows what could happen with a different
government?

00:10:38.290 --> 00:10:40.089
And let’s not forget the drug trafficking.

00:10:40.089 --> 00:10:44.470
According to several DEA reports, between
15 and 20% of all cocaine traffic travels

00:10:44.470 --> 00:10:46.759
through Venezuelan soil.

00:10:46.759 --> 00:10:52.679
Important figures such as DIOSDADO CABELLO
are directly involved in NARCO activities.

00:10:52.679 --> 00:10:56.500
In fact, it’s fair to say that Venezuela
is a narco state.

00:10:56.500 --> 00:11:01.809
A place where traffickers can establish their
logistical hubs with the help of government

00:11:01.809 --> 00:11:02.809
officials.

00:11:02.809 --> 00:11:05.720
OK, all of this sounds good but… the big
question is…

00:11:05.720 --> 00:11:09.269
Can there really be a peaceful democratic
transition in Venezuela?

00:11:09.269 --> 00:11:11.100
We’ll explore that now.

00:11:11.100 --> 00:11:15.040
WHAT CAN BE DONE ABOUT THIS?

00:11:15.040 --> 00:11:18.310
As we said before, Venezuelan opposition is
completely fragmented.

00:11:18.310 --> 00:11:22.170
They have lots of political parties: conservatives,
liberals, socialists...

00:11:22.170 --> 00:11:25.800
But unlike other countries like Poland or
the Czech Republic, where they had strong

00:11:25.800 --> 00:11:30.009
leaders that opposed the dictators, there
is no clear opposition to Maduro.

00:11:30.009 --> 00:11:32.059
But now things have changed.

00:11:32.059 --> 00:11:36.589
With international support, Juan Guaido can
really galvanize the democratic opposition.

00:11:36.589 --> 00:11:38.769
Of course, he’s just the interim president.

00:11:38.769 --> 00:11:41.699
This means, in 30 days, he will have to call
for elections.

00:11:41.699 --> 00:11:45.790
But… this is where the good news ends.

00:11:45.790 --> 00:11:52.889
You see… laws are just empty words if there’s
nobody to enforce them.

00:11:52.889 --> 00:11:55.689
This is why the military and police are so
important.

00:11:55.689 --> 00:11:59.000
In other words, Guaido might have all the
legitimacy he could ever want but…

00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:02.259
How can he call for elections if the army
doesn’t want that to happen?

00:12:02.259 --> 00:12:08.519
This explains why both Guaido and Maduro have
been trying to seduce the army.

00:12:08.519 --> 00:12:15.449
Nicolas Maduro demanded loyalty to the army:
we must enforce the power of the Venezuelan

00:12:15.449 --> 00:12:17.059
nation with the military

00:12:17.059 --> 00:12:18.800
So far, the army is on Maduro’s side.

00:12:18.800 --> 00:12:20.999
At least, at the time we record this video.

00:12:20.999 --> 00:12:26.200
LET’S MAKE A PARENTHESIS HERE: by the time
we are editing this video, this is February,

00:12:26.200 --> 00:12:32.300
2nd, a General from the Venezuelan Army has
uploaded a video to YouTube claiming he supports

00:12:32.300 --> 00:12:36.180
Juan Guaido and rejecting the authority of
Nicolas Maduro.

00:12:36.180 --> 00:12:39.259
His name is Francisco Esteban Yánez.

00:12:39.259 --> 00:12:45.100
You can find the link to the video on the
description box below.

00:12:45.100 --> 00:12:48.040
Most high ranking officials are completely
loyal to his rule.

00:12:48.040 --> 00:12:51.910
And, in the past few years, Caracas has been
raising the salaries of the soldiers.

00:12:51.910 --> 00:12:55.310
Today, the average Venezuelan soldier can
make more money than a surgeon.

00:12:55.310 --> 00:12:57.630
But… still, it’s not that much money.

00:12:57.630 --> 00:13:00.179
In fact, we’re talking about the equivalent
of 80 dollars a month.

00:13:00.179 --> 00:13:04.869
In other words… soldiers are still poor,
like the rest of the country.

00:13:04.869 --> 00:13:07.990
Is this enough to make the army rise against
Maduro?

00:13:07.990 --> 00:13:08.990
We don’t know.

00:13:08.990 --> 00:13:11.050
But it’s something to take into account.

00:13:11.050 --> 00:13:13.439
And what about those high ranking officials?

00:13:13.439 --> 00:13:15.250
Well, they’re another story.

00:13:15.250 --> 00:13:17.759
In fact, they live much better.

00:13:17.759 --> 00:13:19.329
Don’t believe me?

00:13:19.329 --> 00:13:25.660
Let’s take a walk through the SALAMANCA
quarter.

00:13:25.660 --> 00:13:27.529
SALAMANCA is the Spanish Manhattan.

00:13:27.529 --> 00:13:29.939
A Luxury neighbourhood in the center of Madrid.

00:13:29.939 --> 00:13:33.540
Everybody here is pretty well off and… as
a side note, they vote conservative.

00:13:33.540 --> 00:13:36.819
In 2010, only some Venezuelan officials lived
here.

00:13:36.819 --> 00:13:38.431
Some of them even made investments here.

00:13:38.431 --> 00:13:42.180
But in recent years, more and more Maduro
officials have been arriving here.

00:13:42.180 --> 00:13:47.499
In fact, some people are starting to call
this area LITTLE VENEZUELA.

00:13:47.499 --> 00:13:53.360
‘Many times I am in a restaurant here, in
Madrid, and next to me there are people I

00:13:53.360 --> 00:13:59.369
would be scared to see in Caracas’ said
LEOPOLDO LOPEZ GIL, father of LEOPOLDO LOPEZ,

00:13:59.369 --> 00:14:01.199
a Venezuelan political prisoner.

00:14:01.199 --> 00:14:05.399
For example, the personal nurse of Hugo Chavez
bought property for 1.8 M euros in 2015.

00:14:05.399 --> 00:14:09.070
Of course, in cash.

00:14:09.070 --> 00:14:12.629
And just like her, other people have come
with briefcases full of cash, ready to buy

00:14:12.629 --> 00:14:14.220
luxury properties.

00:14:14.220 --> 00:14:16.980
Even the daughter of the Minister of Defense
lives in Madrid.

00:14:16.980 --> 00:14:17.980
In other words…

00:14:17.980 --> 00:14:21.230
Maduro’s officials are sending money to
Venezuela in order to prepare for potential

00:14:21.230 --> 00:14:22.230
exile.

00:14:22.230 --> 00:14:25.769
Some go to Madrid, others go to Miami or Bogota…

00:14:25.769 --> 00:14:28.170
And here’s a good way to put some pressure
on the army.

00:14:28.170 --> 00:14:31.839
Economic sanctions on government officials
would restrict them from making these kinds

00:14:31.839 --> 00:14:32.839
of investments.

00:14:32.839 --> 00:14:34.239
This is nothing new.

00:14:34.239 --> 00:14:37.959
In fact, this is the same policy the international
community has with North Korea.

00:14:37.959 --> 00:14:41.989
These kinds of measures put a lot of pressure
on the military so that they’ll start thinking

00:14:41.989 --> 00:14:44.019
about turning to the democratic side.

00:14:44.019 --> 00:14:48.269
But, OK, OK, what if the army still supports
the dictatorship?

00:14:48.269 --> 00:14:49.600
What could happen here?

00:14:49.600 --> 00:14:52.709
Can a dictatorship survive even if America
doesn’t recognize it?

00:14:52.709 --> 00:14:54.959
The answer is YES.

00:14:54.959 --> 00:15:01.649
For example, MAO ZEDONG’s China was not
recognized by Washington.

00:15:01.649 --> 00:15:05.230
For years, White House considered Taiwan’s
government to be the legitimate government

00:15:05.230 --> 00:15:06.299
of mainland China.

00:15:06.299 --> 00:15:08.519
Something similar could happen here.

00:15:08.519 --> 00:15:10.799
Another possibility is an open civil war.

00:15:10.799 --> 00:15:13.890
The army could fight Guaido, who would ask
for International help.

00:15:13.890 --> 00:15:17.470
In fact, there are rumors that America might
be sending some troops to Colombia.

00:15:17.470 --> 00:15:21.589
Also, we have found news that claims that
some mercenaries have been crossing the border

00:15:21.589 --> 00:15:22.589
from Brazil.

00:15:22.589 --> 00:15:23.589
Is it fake news or not?

00:15:23.589 --> 00:15:24.589
We can’t know for sure.

00:15:24.589 --> 00:15:28.370
But it would make sense.

00:15:28.370 --> 00:15:34.939
Nonetheless, and this is our opinión, it’s
hard to believe that America or Europe would

00:15:34.939 --> 00:15:36.820
risk so much for Venezuela.

00:15:36.820 --> 00:15:39.620
And, Maduro himself doesn’t want a war.

00:15:39.620 --> 00:15:42.990
Civil wars can have unintended consequences
for dictators.

00:15:42.990 --> 00:15:47.509
Especially when they want to leave their presidential
palace overnight and a group of opposers catch

00:15:47.509 --> 00:15:48.589
them.

00:15:48.589 --> 00:15:51.899
Just look at what happened with BENITO MUSSOLINI,
NICOLAE CEAUCESCU, and MUHAMMAR GADDAFI.

00:15:51.899 --> 00:15:56.309
But this is just our opinion… now it’s
your turn.

00:15:56.309 --> 00:15:58.089
What do you think will happen in Venezuela?

00:15:58.089 --> 00:16:01.079
Is it time for this country to recover its
democracy?

00:16:01.079 --> 00:16:03.759
Or will Maduro remain in power for years to
come?

